ACL2 !>
For the admission of FETCH we will use the relation O< (which is known
to be well-founded on the domain recognized by O-P) and the measure
(ACL2-COUNT X).  The non-trivial part of the measure conjecture is

Goal
(IMPLIES (AND (NOT (ENDP P))
              (AND (CONSP X)
                   (INTEGERP (CAR P))
                   (<= 0 (CAR P))
                   (< (CAR P) (LEN X))))
         (O< (ACL2-COUNT (NTH (CAR P) X))
             (ACL2-COUNT X))).
Goal'
Goal''
Goal'''
Goal'4'
Goal'5'

([ A key checkpoint:

Goal''
(IMPLIES (AND (CONSP P)
              (CONSP X)
              (INTEGERP (CAR P))
              (<= 0 (CAR P))
              (< (CAR P) (LEN X)))
         (< (ACL2-COUNT (NTH (CAR P) X))
            (ACL2-COUNT X)))

*1 (Goal'5') is pushed for proof by induction:
(IMPLIES (AND (INTEGERP P1)
              (<= 0 P1)
              (CONSP X)
              (< P1 (LEN X)))
         (< (ACL2-COUNT (NTH P1 X))
            (ACL2-COUNT X))).

])

Perhaps we can prove *1 by induction.  Three induction schemes are
suggested by this conjecture.  Subsumption reduces that number to two.
These merge into one derived induction scheme.  

We will induct according to a scheme suggested by (ACL2-COUNT X), while
accommodating (NTH P1 X) and (LEN X).

These suggestions were produced using the :induction rules ACL2-COUNT,
LEN and NTH.  If we let (:P P1 X) denote *1 above then the induction
scheme we'll use is
(AND (IMPLIES (AND (NOT (CONSP X))
                   (NOT (RATIONALP X))
                   (NOT (COMPLEX-RATIONALP X))
                   (NOT (STRINGP X)))
              (:P P1 X))
     (IMPLIES (AND (NOT (CONSP X))
                   (NOT (RATIONALP X))
                   (NOT (COMPLEX-RATIONALP X))
                   (STRINGP X))
              (:P P1 X))
     (IMPLIES (AND (NOT (CONSP X))
                   (NOT (RATIONALP X))
                   (COMPLEX-RATIONALP X)
                   (:P P1 (REALPART X))
                   (:P P1 (IMAGPART X)))
              (:P P1 X))
     (IMPLIES (AND (NOT (CONSP X))
                   (RATIONALP X)
                   (NOT (INTEGERP X)))
              (:P P1 X))
     (IMPLIES (AND (NOT (CONSP X))
                   (RATIONALP X)
                   (INTEGERP X))
              (:P P1 X))
     (IMPLIES (AND (CONSP X)
                   (:P P1 (CAR X))
                   (:P (+ -1 P1) (CDR X)))
              (:P P1 X))).
This induction is justified by the same argument used to admit ACL2-COUNT.
Note, however, that the unmeasured variable P1 is being instantiated.
When applied to the goal at hand the above induction scheme produces
15 nontautological subgoals.
Subgoal *1/15

